From 31261bd71e2b6a49c1f77f123cf3f6c76d4f5312 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:22:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Port the LiveHime plugin to Windows at the compile layer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The macOS plugin hard-codes Darwin: plugins/livehime/CMakeLists.txt lists 21
Swift files and five .framework libraries unconditionally, so cmake refuses to
configure on Windows. The session core behind the Qt UI is Swift and imports
WebKit, CryptoKit, Security, AppKit, ImageIO, UniformTypeIdentifiers,
AVFoundation, Speech, CoreMedia, CoreImage and Compression with no #if os()
fallback anywhere; the window layer is Objective-C++.

Compile layer only — no session logic is implemented here:

  plugins/livehime/CMakeLists.txt   select core/ and the window layer per
                                    platform instead of assuming Darwin
  plugins/livehime/src/window-native.cpp
                                    Windows window behaviour (topmost level,
                                    SetWindowDisplayAffinity, HWND ids, the
                                    capture-exception proc)
  plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core-stub.cpp
                                    all 35 livehime_core_* entry points,
                                    reporting "unsupported"; the UI links and
                                    loads, the features do not
  build-aux/livehime-win/build-win.ps1
                                    Windows counterpart of build-macos.sh

Branding, icon and config isolation, mirroring patch 0001 on macOS:

  cmake/windows/defaults.cmake      LIVEHIME_APP_NAME / _DISPLAY_NAME /
                                    _COMPANY_NAME / _APP_ICON and
                                    OBS_USER_CONFIG_SUBDIR cache variables,
                                    defaults reproducing upstream exactly
  frontend/cmake/windows/obs.rc.in  version resource from those variables
  cmake/windows/livehime-win.ico    from livehime-appicon.svg, six sizes
  libobs/cmake/os-windows.cmake     OBS_USER_CONFIG_SUBDIR compile definition
  libobs/util/platform-windows.c    user_config_subdir(): per-user paths gain
                                    the subdirectory, %PROGRAMDATA% untouched

The executable stays obs64.exe; only the product identity changes. Nothing has
been built on Windows yet — see docs/WINDOWS_PORT.md.
